From 31a34885388835dce2460744d7961f2b9e7dc416 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Filip Dumitru <filip.stefan.dumitru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:56:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: ov9282: Arm FSIN wake last in external trigger
 setup

ov9282_apply_trigger_config() sets the FSIN wake bit in
LOW_POWER_MODE_CTRL (0x3030) before it writes NUM_FRAME_ON_TRIG, the
sleep period and TIMING_23 (no auto wake). FSIN comes from an external
source and is not gated while the driver is setting up, so an edge
that arrives after the arm write but before the rest of the sequence
wakes the sensor with those registers still at their power-on defaults.
When that happens the sensor can be left free-running at its internal
frame rate and ignore FSIN until the next stream start.

Write the arm bit last, once everything the wake path depends on is
already set. Nothing else changes.

On a stereo pair of OV9281 modules on a Raspberry Pi 5 (6.18.34),
triggered at 30 Hz, with an msleep(100) added just after the point
where the stock driver arms so that edges always land inside the
window:

  arm bit   free-running starts
  early     12/40
  last       0/40

Without the forced delay, neither ordering failed in 80 starts. The
natural window (arm write to end of setup) is about 2 ms with the
stock order.

Link: https://github.com/raspberrypi/linux/issues/5349
Fixes: 01732af7d1a3 ("media: i2c: ov9282: Add external FSIN trigger snapshot mode")
Signed-off-by: Filip Dumitru <filip.stefan.dumitru@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/ov9282.c | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov9282.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov9282.c
@@ -985,11 +985,6 @@ static int ov9282_apply_trigger_config(s
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	/* External trigger snapshot */
-	ret = ov9282_write_reg(ov9282, OV9282_REG_LOW_POWER_MODE_CTRL, 1, 0x04);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
-
 	/* 1 frame per trigger */
 	ret = ov9282_write_reg(ov9282, OV9282_REG_NUM_FRAME_ON_TRIG, 1, 0x01);
 	if (ret)
@@ -1008,6 +1003,11 @@ static int ov9282_apply_trigger_config(s
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/* External trigger snapshot */
+	ret = ov9282_write_reg(ov9282, OV9282_REG_LOW_POWER_MODE_CTRL, 1, 0x04);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
